THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

A compiled Boobook binary statically links third-party libraries that remain
under their own licences, which this notice neither replaces nor restricts. A
distributed binary must carry their notices too.

Every one of them is listed, with its licence text, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
All are permissive — MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC — apart from one file-scoped
copyleft licence, MPL-2.0.

The principal components are the embedded DuckDB database
(github.com/duckdb/duckdb-go, MIT), the Windows event log and registry hive
parsers (www.velocidex.com/golang/evtx and .../regparser, Apache-2.0) and the
compound file parsers behind jump list reading (github.com/richardlehane/mscfb
and .../msoleps, Apache-2.0).

Regenerate THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md whenever the dependency set changes; the list
is the modules reachable from `go list -deps ./cmd/boobook`, not the whole
go.mod graph.
